 "id": "clock/read-beats-clock-past-ttl/hot",
 "description": "r0 writes a 5m entry (5,000 tokens). r1 comes 5 minutes 30 seconds later, 30 seconds past the TTL, and the provider billed a read of the whole entry: read 5,000, write 500. The provider measures the TTL from the end of the previous response, so a long streamed response can put the entry inside the TTL. The billed read is the evidence, and it beats the clock at any gap: the phase is hot and the replayed 2,000 tokens are read (2,000 x $0.30/M). Before the fix the margin was 10 seconds and the phase was cold.",
